---
/**
 * A NUMBERED SECTION BREAK inside a chapter.
 *
 *   <SectionMark />          ->  I, then II, then III, in document order
 *   <SectionMark title="…" /> ->  the numeral with a title under it
 *
 * The author writes chapters in numbered movements rather than titled ones:
 * a section is not a topic with a name, it is a turn in one argument, and the
 * numeral is the whole of its identity. This renders that turn.
 *
 * IT IS AN `<h2>`, not a decorated `<p>`. Three things depend on that and all
 * three are real: the document outline (a screen reader moving by heading must
 * find the same three movements a sighted reader sees), the running head in
 * ChapterLayout (which reads `.prose h2` and would otherwise report nothing
 * for the whole chapter), and the id, which makes a movement linkable —
 * `#sec-ii` is a citable address for a section that has no name to link by.
 * The word "Section" is present for the heading's accessible name and hidden
 * from the page, where the numeral's size and isolation already say it.
 *
 * NO RULE, DELIBERATELY. The obvious design is a hairline across the measure
 * with the numeral sitting on it, and the rules doctrine in tokens.css
 * forbids exactly that — "a rule above every heading is scaffolding left in
 * the build". What separates the movements here is what the doctrine says
 * should: space, and a change of register from the 18px working face to a
 * document-face numeral. Nothing is joined, so nothing needs dividing.
 *
 * CENTRED, AND IT IS THE ONE THING ON THE PAGE THAT IS. Every other element
 * shares the main column's left edge, because everything else is read in
 * sequence and a second left edge costs the eye a re-anchor. A section
 * numeral is not read in sequence — it is looked at once, on the way past —
 * and centring is what a book does with an unnamed movement for exactly that
 * reason: it reads as a rest rather than as the start of a line. It is also
 * what keeps the numeral clear of the margin column, where sidenotes float
 * and would land on it.
 *
 * The numeral is TRACKED HARD, at a quarter of an em. Roman numerals are
 * repeated strokes — II, III, XI — and at text spacing they close into a
 * picket fence that has to be counted rather than read. Centring makes the
 * tracking free: there is no left edge for the extra space to break.
 *
 * SIZE IS RESTRAINED ON PURPOSE. It sat at 36px, which put a numeral between
 * the h2 and the title in weight and made every movement look like a new
 * chapter. At the h2's size with this much air around it, the space does the
 * announcing and the numeral only has to be found.
 */
import { nextSectionNumber, roman } from '../lib/section-counter';

interface Props {
  /**
   * Optional. A movement can carry a name as well as a numeral; most do not,
   * and the design is built for the bare numeral rather than tolerating it.
   */
  title?: string;
  /** Overrides the derived id, which is `sec-` plus the lowercased numeral. */
  id?: string;
}

const n = nextSectionNumber(Astro.request);
const numeral = roman(n);
const { title, id = `sec-${numeral.toLowerCase()}` } = Astro.props;
---

<h2 class="sectionmark" id={id}>
  <span class="u-sr-only">Section </span><span class="sectionmark__numeral">{numeral}</span
  >{title && <span class="sectionmark__title">{title}</span>}
</h2>

<style>
  .sectionmark {
    /* The break is the space. 128px above and 64px below — the numeral
       belongs to the movement it opens, not to the one it closes, which is
       the same asymmetry every heading on the site uses, opened up because
       this break is the largest one a chapter has. */
    margin-block: var(--space-10) var(--space-8);
    text-align: center;
    /* Landing on `#sec-ii` must not park the numeral against the top edge of
       the viewport, and the sticky running head sits there too. */
    scroll-margin-block-start: var(--space-8);
  }

  /* A chapter that opens on its first movement — this one does — must not
     start with 128px of nothing above the numeral. The header already owns
     that clearing. */
  .sectionmark:first-child {
    margin-block-start: 0;
  }

  .sectionmark__numeral {
    display: block;
    font-family: var(--font-doc);
    font-size: var(--type-h2-size);
    line-height: 1;
    /* The tracking adds a quarter-em after the last stroke as well as between
       them, which pulls an optically centred numeral to the left. The indent
       gives it back. */
    letter-spacing: 0.25em;
    text-indent: 0.25em;
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  .sectionmark__title {
    display: block;
    /* Set from the numeral's own tracked line rather than the paragraph
       below, so numeral and title read as one mark. */
    margin-block-start: var(--space-4);
    font-size: var(--type-h2-size);
    line-height: var(--type-h2-leading);
    letter-spacing: -0.005em;
    color: var(--ink);
  }
</style>
